Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Exclusive housekeeping; validate restore uploads and keep
 the previous DB

- Housekeeping (with VACUUM) starts only when no other command runs, and a
  queued housekeeping never holds back other commands.
- A restore upload must be a Radarr database (or a valid config); other
  files are rejected with a 4xx instead of replacing the live database.
- The previous database is kept as radarr.db.pre-restore* until startup
  after the restore succeeds, and moved back if the final move fails.
